=== Anamorph DSP self-tests ===
Test 1: MS encode/decode round-trip
  max round-trip error = 1.788e-07
Test 2: no NaN / Inf / denormals across feature matrix
Test 3+4: true-bypass null + latency reporting
  bypass null max diff (OS off) = 0.000e+00
  OS factor latency=4, impulse peak at 4
  OS factor latency=6, impulse peak at 6
  OS factor latency=6, impulse peak at 6
Test 5: default parameters are transparent
  default transparency max diff = 5.960e-08
Test 6: Mono Maker collapses low-frequency side energy
  side RMS  on=0.0057  off=0.7019
  mono-low Mid RMS on=0.7080 (expect ~0.70)
Test 7: Multiband preserves the mono sum across Mix (phase fix)
  Mix=0.25 mono-sum RMS out/in = 1.000 (expect ~1.0; unaligned dry combs to <0.8)
  Mix=0.50 mono-sum RMS out/in = 1.000 (expect ~1.0; unaligned dry combs to <0.8)
  Mix=0.75 mono-sum RMS out/in = 1.000 (expect ~1.0; unaligned dry combs to <0.8)
Test 8: Mono Maker (post-Mix) collapses the low Side at any Mix
  Mix=0.25  output low-Side / input = 0.009 (expect << 1)
  Mix=0.50  output low-Side / input = 0.010 (expect << 1)
  Mix=0.75  output low-Side / input = 0.011 (expect << 1)
Test 9: Band Solo is a post-everything band-pass monitor
  100Hz: band0 0.643 band3 0.000 ; 6kHz: band3 0.671 band0 0.000
  energy  no-solo 3381.9  all-bands-solo 3343.9 (ratio 0.989, expect ~1)
Test 10: Level Match works and is solo-independent
  match gain  solo off -3.51 dB  solo band0 -3.51 dB
Test 11: no clicks across Solo / Mix / Gain / Balance / A-B / Reset
  max sample-to-sample delta = 0.0123 (clean-sine slew ~0.008) ; max |out| = 0.260
Test 12: toggling Band Solo in silence emits no ghost signal
  max |out| over silent solo toggles = 0.00e+00
Test 13: Level Match reads ~0 at unity (no bias)
  unity match gain = -0.000 dB (expect ~0)
Test 14: Level Match predict doesn't ratchet on repeated Drive up/down (paused)
  most-negative paused predict = -12.00 dB ; final (drive 24) = -12.00 dB
Test 15: Mix feeds the predict; pause->Mix-up->play doesn't slam
  dry match=-0.12 dB ; Mix100 steady peak=0.563 ; first played peak=0.590 (ratio 1.05)
Test 16: Level Match holds its value on silence (measure waits)
  converged=-4.30 dB ; after 1 s silence=-4.53 dB
Test 17: Multiband crossover automation is Nyquist-safe (no explosion)
  sr=44100  max|out|=1.814
  sr=48000  max|out|=1.832
  sr=96000  max|out|=1.504
Test 18: Level Match reads ~0 at unity with Multiband ON
  multiband-on unity match = -0.000 dB (expect ~0)
Test 19: meters self-heal after a NaN/Inf burst
  bright reading after recovery = -7.35 dB (expect ~ -6)
Test 20: bypass toggling is clean (no burst; silent-in -> silent-out)
  settled bypass silent-in tail = 0.00e+00 ; play-toggle max|out| = 2.020
Test 21: Level Match keeps measuring while bypassed
  match: active -5.62 dB  bypassed -5.62 dB
Test 22: bypass crossfade is click-free and never mutes
  max delta=0.0072 ; min block peak=0.125 (processed 0.125 .. bypass 0.25)
Test 23: Multiband Enable crossfade is click-free and never mutes
  max delta=0.0099 ; min block peak=0.200
Test 24: Band Solo + Multiband Enable toggle is click-free
  max delta=0.0147 ; min block peak=0.292
Test 25: dry-align gate (H4) -- aggregate mono RMS through Mix re-entry
  transition mono-sum RMS out/in = 0.999, settled = 1.000 (unaligned combs to <0.8)
Test 26: a forced bulk swap (undo / A-B / preset) never dips to silence
  continuous bulk swap (width/mix): min 2 ms window RMS across the swap = 0.931 of steady (pre-fix ~0)
  algorithm bulk swap (velvet -> haas): min 2 ms window RMS across the swap = 0.651 of steady (pre-fix ~0)
Test 27: rapid consecutive forced swaps re-evaluate dry-fill (no stale state)
  neutral -> neutral (control): min 2 ms window RMS through swap2 = 0.930 of steady (stale-state engine ~0)
  latency-cross -> neutral (re-enable dry-fill): min 2 ms window RMS through swap2 = 1.149 of steady (stale-state engine ~0)
  neutral -> latency-cross during fade-IN (disable dry-fill, no wrong-offset read): min 2 ms window RMS through swap2 = 0.004 of steady (stale-state engine ~0)
  neutral -> latency-cross during fade-OUT (tighten branch): min 2 ms window RMS through swap2 = 0.000 of steady (stale-state engine ~0)
Test 28: multiband reconstruction is flat (no EQ dip at close crossovers)
  4-band, three close splits (800/1000/1250)   worst deviation = -0.00 dB (pre-fix close splits combed to -17 dB)
  4-band, very close (900/1000/1100)           worst deviation = -0.00 dB (pre-fix close splits combed to -17 dB)
  4-band, wide (200/1000/5000)                 worst deviation = -0.00 dB (pre-fix close splits combed to -17 dB)
  3-band (500/2000)                            worst deviation = -0.00 dB (pre-fix close splits combed to -17 dB)
  2-band (single crossover)                    worst deviation = -0.00 dB (pre-fix close splits combed to -17 dB)
Test 29: fast split drags do not pitch-shift (multiband + solo monitor)
  multiband:    worst pitch deviation = 14.04 cents (uncapped: 28+, one-pole: ~50); max delta = 0.0049
  crawl-cross:  worst pitch deviation = 14.00 cents (uncapped: 28+, one-pole: ~50); max delta = 0.0049
  multiband:    max spur while the split crosses a 1 kHz tone = -41.3 dBc (chained fades: ~-26; threshold -31)
  solo monitor: worst pitch deviation = 14.24 cents (uncapped: 28+, one-pole: ~50); max delta = 0.0049
  convergence:  level 1.7-2.2 s after a 6-oct flick = 0.16 of full (1.25 oct/s follower: ~1.0)
  discrete 4-oct jump: level at +200..350 ms = 1.00 of full (crawl would be ~0.004); max delta = 0.0326
  normal drag:  solo band edge at +100..350 ms after release = 0.99 of full (flat 4 oct/s cap: ~0.5); max delta = 0.1287
  normal drag:  multiband width-0 leak at +100..350 ms after release = 0.01 of the leak level (flat cap: ~0.9)
Test 30: forced-swap dry fill respects extreme Output Gain (no spike)
  steady peak at -24 dB = 0.0158 ; worst transition peak = 0.0158 (1.0x; raw-level fill spiked ~15x)
Test 31: a forced swap during an ordinary fade-out keeps forced semantics
  A: max |out| after the silent bottom (silent input) = 0.000000 (pre-fix 0.494: stale Haas tail replays)
  B: max sample delta 0.0072 (sine slope ~0.0072); duck floor 0.000 of steady; recovery 0.996 of steady
Test 32: high-rate crossover snap lands exactly (192 kHz float stall)
  sr  44100: mb gaps +0.0000 +0.0000 +0.0000 Hz; solo gaps +0.0000 +0.0000 +0.0000 Hz; cold=1 (pre-fix @192k: 0.47/0.94/1.87 short, never cold)
  sr  48000: mb gaps +0.0000 +0.0000 +0.0000 Hz; solo gaps +0.0000 +0.0000 +0.0000 Hz; cold=1 (pre-fix @192k: 0.47/0.94/1.87 short, never cold)
  sr  96000: mb gaps +0.0000 +0.0000 +0.0000 Hz; solo gaps +0.0000 +0.0000 +0.0000 Hz; cold=1 (pre-fix @192k: 0.47/0.94/1.87 short, never cold)
  sr 192000: mb gaps +0.0000 +0.0000 +0.0000 Hz; solo gaps +0.0000 +0.0000 +0.0000 Hz; cold=1 (pre-fix @192k: 0.47/0.94/1.87 short, never cold)
  192k top zone: mb gap +0.0000 Hz; solo gap +0.0000 Hz; cold=1 (pre-fix: 3.75 short, never cold)
